  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a suru verb ({明記|めいき}する) or noun. Very common in instructions on forms, contracts, and official documents. The pattern {明記|めいき}の{上|うえ} means 'having clearly stated' and is standard in application instructions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～を{明記|めいき}する: to clearly state ~\n- {明記|めいき}の{上|うえ}: having clearly noted (on documents)\n- ～に{明記|めいき}されている: is clearly stated in ~\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {明示|めいじ}: explicit indication (showing clearly, not necessarily in writing)\n- {記載|きさい}: entry, description (writing down, less emphasis on clarity)",
